[stderr] ```
[stderr] 
[stderr] After the parent completes, `--run-all` follows each registered child collection
[stderr] recursively. This is explicit by design: Supervisor never scans and executes
[stderr] arbitrary directories. Named-project collection state is stored in that
[stderr] workspace's `.state/` directory, so generated task IDs such as `R0001` remain
[stderr] isolated across projects. Set `SUPERVISOR_DATABASE_PATH` only when deliberately
[stderr] sharing state.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Updating project configuration safely
[stderr] 
[stderr] `supervisor update` fast-forwards the project-owned `supervisor/` checkout,
[stderr] reinstalls its CLI, then runs the newly downloaded version's environment
[stderr] migrations. The authoritative, append-only history is committed to the
[stderr] Supervisor repository in `supervisor/env_migrations.json`. `supervisor update`
[stderr] compares that manifest with `SUPERVISOR_ENV_SCHEMA_VERSION` in the project's
[stderr] private project-root `.env`, adds missing safe defaults or declared renamed keys, and never
[stderr] overwrites an existing project value.
