---

## Objective

Close the one incomplete design-evidence boundary found by `GC0001`: the
finite QB-A catalogue has a grammar, source policy, quota tables, lifecycle,
adjudication, and anti-repeat fixtures, but `QB-A-01` through `QB-A-48` are
still `draft` and have only pending reviews. Create or review durable editorial
acceptance evidence for the existing four bounded batches only. Do not add
cards, change quiz scope, create code/B/R runbooks, or accept the manifest.

## Exact pending reasons retained from GC0001

- `GPI-001`: the grammar requires a resolvable provenance record and two
  distinct accepted current-revision reviews, but it contains no completed
  card-level records for `QB-A-01`–`QB-A-48`.
- `GPI-002`, `GPI-003`, `GPI-004`, and `GPI-005`: each of the four named
  12-card QB-A batches is explicitly recorded as `status: draft`,
  `revision: 1`, with `PROV-<ID>` and two pending review records. No card may
  become eligible from those placeholders.
- `GAME-002`: the required original-expression, factual-source/provenance,
  factual/rights review, accessibility/copy review, and independent second
  review decisions have not been accepted for any current card revision.
- `GAME-004` and `GAME-006` retain their deterministic policy/fixture evidence,
  but their use of published catalogue candidates remains conditional until the
  preceding batch records are accepted.

There are no blocked product decisions in this wave. Implementation coverage
remains deferred until `F012`.

## Output list

- `design-evidence/qba-editorial-acceptance-register.md`: exactly 48
  card-level records for the existing `QB-A-01`–`QB-A-48`, grouped into the
  existing four named 12-card batches. Each record must identify the current
  revision, original-expression/non-copying decision, durable permitted source
  locator and checked date for every factual assertion, conflict/correction
  state, factual/rights review, accessibility/copy review, independent second
  review, and resulting lifecycle status.
- Update `design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md` only as
  needed to point to the register and replace the explicitly pending catalogue
  state after all 48 records qualify. Preserve its existing quotas, IDs, and
  source policy.

The successor must leave rejected, unresolved, withdrawn, conflicted, or
incompletely reviewed cards ineligible and state the exact reason. It must not
set `planning/game-design-manifest.json` to accepted. A later `GQ` audit is the
only task allowed to run the dedicated completion check, update canonical
bible/inventory records, and accept that manifest.

## Acceptance criteria

- All 48 existing QB-A card revisions have independently inspectable
  original-expression, provenance, and two-distinct-review evidence, or every
  remaining ineligible card has its exact pending or blocked reason retained.
- The four existing batches remain finite at 12 cards each and no unreviewed
  record can enter selection.

